## Cooperating with the narrator (read once)

- The narrator owns **the world and the clock**: NPCs speak, time passes, consequences arrive. You own **what she chooses**.
- A short turn means "keep going": the narrator may move time and bring people in. A long turn means "I'm driving": the narrator follows.
- There is no "right script". A chapter has one exit and many doors; the door you invent is the winning one.
- Periodic bakes (`/st-arc-save`) lock what you wrote into the lorebook as fact. This brief is refreshed at every bake.
